  "text": "To find the value of the given determinant, we first rewrite the determinant with a factor of \\(\\sin \\alpha + \\cos \\alpha\\) in the first row:\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} \n\\cos^2 \\alpha & \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha & \\sin^2 \\alpha \\\\ \n\\cos^2 \\beta & \\cos \\beta \\sin \\beta & \\sin^2 \\beta \\\\ \n\\cos^2 \\gamma & \\cos \\gamma \\sin \\gamma & \\sin^2 \\gamma \n\\end{vmatrix}\n=\n\\sin \\alpha (\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta + \\sin \\beta \\cos \\alpha) + \\cos \\alpha (\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta + \\sin^2 \\beta) + \\sin(\\gamma)(\\cos^2 \\gamma + \\sin^2 \\gamma) \n\\]\n\\[\n= 2 \\sin(\\alpha + \\beta) + \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma + \\sin \\gamma\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\left\\{ \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma + \\sin \\gamma \\right\\} + 2 \\sin \\gamma \\sin(\\alpha + \\beta)\n\\]\n\\[\n=\\sin \\gamma \\left( \\cos \\alpha + 1 + 2 \\sin(\\alpha + \\beta) \\right)\n\\]\n\nBy symmetry, we can replace \\(\\alpha\\) with \\(\\beta\\) and \\(\\beta\\) with \\(\\gamma\\):\n\\[\n= \\sin \\gamma \\left[ \\left( 2 \\sin(\\beta + \\gamma) - \\cos \\gamma \\right) - \\cos \\gamma + 2 \\sin(\\gamma + \\alpha) \\right]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sin \\gamma \\left( 4 \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 8 \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma\n\\]\n\nConsidering the factor \\(1 \\cdot \\left( \\sin \\alpha + \\cos \\alpha \\right)\\), we have:\n\\[\n= 8 \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma \\cdot 1 = 4 \\cdot 2 \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma\n\\]\n\nIn fact, we can prove the exact value by considering the inverse cosine property. Therefore, the value of the determinant is \n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n concluding that the value of the given determinant is 1.",
